From 2e14ffbb253a56711aae45daf369ffb17bc56f66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:15:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: connac: bound the scan IEs in
 mt76_connac_mcu_hw_scan()

mt76_connac_mcu_hw_scan() copies sreq->ie into the fixed ies[] array of
the request without a check. With SINGLE_SCAN_ON_ALL_BANDS, mac80211
passes the IEs of all bands in one buffer, and copies the custom IEs
that must precede the band capabilities once per band, but
max_scan_ie_len only bounds the IEs from userspace. A multi-band scan
with large IEs thus overruns ies[] into the fields behind it. Reachable
via NL80211_CMD_TRIGGER_SCAN on mt7921, and on mt7615 with firmware
offload.

Reject such a request, like nl80211 rejects IEs above max_scan_ie_len.

Fixes: fcdfc29e58ee ("mt76: mt7615: introduce hw scan support")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 mt76_connac_mcu.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt76_connac_mcu.c b/mt76_connac_mcu.c
index c1d67024..bf909eaf 100644
--- a/mt76_connac_mcu.c
+++ b/mt76_connac_mcu.c
@@ -1823,6 +1823,10 @@ int mt76_connac_mcu_hw_scan(struct mt76_phy *phy, struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
 	if (test_bit(MT76_HW_SCANNING, &phy->state))
 		return -EBUSY;
 
+	/* max_scan_ie_len does not cover the per-band IEs of all bands */
+	if (sreq->ie_len > sizeof(req->ies))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	skb = mt76_mcu_msg_alloc(mdev, NULL, sizeof(*req));
 	if (!skb)
 		return -ENOMEM;
